From 8926f3364750c44c405c24c905bde89e96c54ffd Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Chris Willingham <clwillingham@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 26 Jan 2026 18:05:57 -0600
Subject: [PATCH 01/12] workspace: Implement more per-monitor workspace support

- Enhanced the Workspace class to handle workspace activation based on the monitor in per-monitor mode.
- Updated the WorkspaceAnimationController to manage workspace animations specific to the monitor.
- Modified the MonitorWorkspaceSwitcherPopup to display workspaces relevant to the current monitor.
- Adjusted WorkspaceThumbnail to ensure window management aligns with the active workspace on the respective monitor.
- Refined the ThumbnailsBox to filter and display workspaces based on the monitor context.
- Improved WorkspacesView to manage workspace visibility and scrolling adjustments according to the active workspace on the monitor.
- Added error handling and logging for better debugging in workspace management.
- Ensured compatibility with existing global workspace functionality while introducing per-monitor features.

For [Issue 37](https://gitlab.gnome.org/GNOME/mutter/-/issues/37)
