From 0ab810250a1a77ca2a09a24fce947f72db13bbdb Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: "Victor C." <34163765+vicajilau@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 21 Aug 2026 07:11:12 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 07/12] workspaceAnimation: Only touch the monitor that
 switches workspace

Switching workspace on one monitor made the others visibly move and jump
back. _prepareWorkspaceSwitch() built a MonitorGroup for every monitor,
which reparents that monitor's windows into it, and the group was then
destroyed without ever being animated.

Build a group only for the monitor that switches, and for the monitor a
swipe gesture started on.

The groups were also built from workspace indices, which are the
position of a workspace within its own monitor, and looked them back up
with get_workspace_by_index(), which counts every workspace. A group for
the second monitor was therefore filled with the workspaces of the
first. Hand the workspaces themselves over instead, so there is no index
to misinterpret.
