Subject: [PATCH 10/12] windowManager: Switch the workspaces of the monitor
 being used

Of the three ways _showWorkspaceSwitcher() picks a workspace, only the
directional one asked the monitor being used. The numbered shortcuts
indexed into the list of every workspace, and "switch to last workspace"
took the last of them all.

With per-monitor workspaces that list holds every monitor's workspaces
one after another, so switching to workspace 3 landed on the third
workspace of the first monitor no matter which monitor the pointer was
on, and switching to the last one always landed on the last workspace of
the last monitor.

Resolve all three against the workspaces of the monitor being used. That
also fixes the early return for a single workspace, which counted every
workspace rather than the ones of that monitor.
